<title>POLAND: Polish industrial output down 5.7 pct in May.</title>
<headline>Polish industrial output down 5.7 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output (unadjusted) fell 5.7 percent in May after a 6.0 percent rise in April, and was 6.6 percent higher than in May 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>Industrial output in the January-May period rose 9.2 percent against the same period of 1996.  </p>
<p> POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	    MAY	APRIL	MAY 1996</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	     -5.7	 +6.0	   2.4</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)			6.6	+15.9	   8.9</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)	 128.4	135.4	   N.A</p>
<p> mining m/m change			-8.8	  3.9(4.7)   -7.5</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change		    -0.7	  1.9(2.7)   -3.7</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	     -4.3	  7.5(7.4)    5.6</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change	    7.3	 18.6(18.5)  12.0</p>
<p> utilities m/m change		   -5.4	 -4.2	 -15.0</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change		  5.3	  5.8(5.9)   -5.8</p>
<p>NOTES - May 1996 and 1997 had 21 working days and April 1996 had 23 working days. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
